# PART 7 – BACKEND API IMPLEMENTATION

Implement complete REST APIs using the existing Express architecture.

Suggested endpoints:

## Teacher Code

GET /api/teacher/connections/code

Returns the authenticated teacher's code information.

POST /api/teacher/connections/code

Generates a code if none exists.

POST /api/teacher/connections/code/regenerate

Revokes the previous code and creates a new one.

POST /api/teacher/connections/code/deactivate

Deactivates the current code.

## Parent Code Validation

POST /api/parent/teacher-connections/validate-code

Input:
- code.

Returns:
- valid status.
- limited teacher public information.
- code expiration status.

Never return sensitive teacher information.

## Parent Requests

GET /api/parent/teacher-connections

Returns the authenticated parent's requests and approved connections.

POST /api/parent/teacher-connections/requests

Input:
- childId.
- code.

Validates ownership and creates a pending request.

DELETE /api/parent/teacher-connections/requests/:requestId

Cancels an authorized pending request.

DELETE /api/parent/teacher-connections/:connectionId

Disconnects an authorized active relationship.

## Teacher Requests

GET /api/teacher/connections/requests

Returns pending requests belonging to the authenticated teacher.

POST /api/teacher/connections/requests/:requestId/approve

Approves a pending request.

POST /api/teacher/connections/requests/:requestId/reject

Rejects a pending request.

GET /api/teacher/connections/students

Returns approved connected students.

DELETE /api/teacher/connections/students/:connectionId

Disconnects an authorized relationship where permitted.

Adapt endpoint naming if the existing project uses another consistent convention.

Implement:
- Request validation.
- Response validation.
- Consistent HTTP status codes.
- Error handling.
- Authentication middleware.
- Authorization middleware.
- Rate limiting.
- CSRF protection.
- Audit logging.

All endpoints must use the existing authenticated session and security architecture.

Never trust teacherId or parentId supplied by the frontend.

Derive authenticated identities from the server-side session.

